rs for an ultra violent  sealist character from dark force comics  despite the masks insane profitability  the only sequel was 2005's  horrible misfire son of the mask which  tanked with 59 million  on a 100 million budget  [Music]  carrie wisely sat that one out an  unsurprising choice giving his  long-standing distaste for sequels  however it sounds like the star may be  open to putting back on the mask as he  told comicbooknews.com in 2020  it would depend on a filmmaker i don't  want to just do it  but i would only do it if it was some  crazy visionary filmmaker  so granted carrie sounds reluctant about  the whole deal but there were rumors in  2020 that warner  brothers was considering both a  female-led reboot more in line with the  darker comic  and two new mask movies starring carrie  since then there haven't been any  updates on this potential franchise  and until carrie warms to the idea it's  doubtful  there ever will be both basic instinct  movies drew in  a bunch of money at the box office with  the first one earning 117 million  dollars domestically and 352 million  dollars worldwide in 1992 despite its  mediocre critical reception  and while strike while the irons haunt  may not be a  basic human instinct it is hollywood's  mantra making it all the more surprising  that it took  14 years for basic instinct 2 to arrive  on screens  michael douglas was out this time but  sharon stone returned as the psychotic  novelist catherine trammell  while the first movie made stone a star  however the sequel  probably killed any chance of her  headlining a film again  it tanked with the critics and did  nothing for audiences either bringing in  35 million  box office on a 70 million dollar budget  you'd think that have killed the  franchise stone  dead but according to a 2006 empire  online article  stone was optimistic about a sequel and  she even hopes to direct  she said there's a script for the next  part of the story but i would like to  direct it rather than star in it  according to a 2013 huffpost article  stone has changed her mind about not  starring in the film and is still  eager to give tremel closure in crank  jason statham has to keep his adrenaline  going to stay alive  by any means necessary in crank 2 high  voltage  statham's heart is replaced with a  battery that needs constant jolts of  electricity  what would have happened in crank 3  sadly  we'll never know crank cost 12 million  dollars and made 43 million dollars  worldwide  q sql crank 2 high voltage cost 20  million dollars and made 35 million  dollars worldwide  so game over right well co-director mark  neville dean was confident the franchise  would keep going telling empire online  in 2011  crank 3 is going to happen the studios  are really excited about it  it's just all about timing four years  later statham told we got this covered  i'd love to do it neville dean and  co-creator brian taylor have to get  their heads together and if they want to  do it then there's a conversation  in 2018 taylor told the movie crypt  podcast that given crank 2's  disappointing box office  it's got to be a great idea something  insane crank 3 should be as  exponentially more  dup than crank 2 as crank 2 was with  crank 1.  the blues brothers was one of the best  comedies of its  era and blues brothers 2000 was among  the worst snl movies ever  nearly 20 years separated these two  movies but given the sequel lacked john  belushi or  you know any redeeming value it  absolutely tanked earning just 14  million dollars at the box office  about 17 years later commemorating the  original's 35th anniversary dan  aykroyd told cbs news that if universal  ever wanted to make a third film  i have a story of course but it involves  handing it off to a younger generation  acroid was even more emphatic in a 2015  interview with the daily mail  telling the outlet that the blues  brothers will return for a dvd  and video on demand special with jim  belushi stepping in for his late brother  aykroyd said the focus will be on  ellwood helping find a new generation  to lead the blues and that idea is  handing down to a new generation  finding a pair of girls who are 20 21  and one to be the blues sisters  in a 2018 interview with et canada  aykroyd even revealed his dreamcast for  this sequel saying  i like lupita nyong'o and i like taylor  swift  whether the blues sisters ever comes to  pass however is pretty much  anybody's guess check out one of our  newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite movie series are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one
 

